1.9672.463Burrows relates to "an aircraft lavatory with a movable or pivotal wall." Burrows atSVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1530.09[0002]. Burrows states, at paragraph [0037], that "as shown in FIG. 3, before the firstwall 16 is pivoted, the lavatory monument assembly 10 defines a first passenger footprint F1.... [and a]s shown in FIG. 3A, after the first wall 16 is pivoted, the lavatory monument assembly 10 defines a second passenger footprint F2, which has a larger area than the first passenger footprint F1." However, while Burrows discusses two configurations, Applicant respectfully submits that Burrows is silent to Applicant respectfully submits that Burrows fails to disclose a lavatory unit that is PRM-accessible, much less "wherein the lavatory unit is configurable between an able-bodied configuration and a PRM- accessible configuration, in which the PRM-accessible configuration of the lavatory unit accommodates (i) a PRM in a wheelchair and allows for a transfer from the wheelchair to the toilet, and (ii) an assistant when one is required by a PRM,"

Respectfully submitted, /Marlena F. Burt/SVG
